  "title": "The Lamplighter's Ledger",
  "subtitle": "A Mystery of Gas and Shadows",
  "authorDisplayName": "Liszt Think",
  "description": "London, November 1887. Three gas lamps on Commercial Road were logged as lit on a night the lamplighter swore he never walked. A week later, he is found dead in the Regent's Canal. The only witness is the ledger itself. Ada Quill, a clerk at the Gas Light and Coke Company, keeps the lamplighters' rounds ledger—and she notices what the police would rather overlook. Every entry tells a story; the discrepancy points to murder. As Ada traces the routes through company offices, the Beckton gasworks, and the fog-shrouded streets, she discovers the clues were always there in the meter readings. Someone profited from a lamp that burned all night, and someone is willing to kill to keep the books closed. A fair-play mystery where the reader sees every entry Ada sees, the solution turns on the mechanics of Victorian gas lighting, and a quiet clerk must decide whether to bring the truth into the light.",
