  "editorReview": {
    "text": "The Victorian gasworks are rendered with such atmospheric precision—you can practically hear the mantle hum and feel the coal-dust—that the setting becomes a character in itself. Ada Quill is a compelling protagonist, her deductive process grounded in satisfying fair-play clues and a unique numerical mindset. However, the prose occasionally slips into mechanical patterns, with repetitive sentence openings and overwrought gas-lamp imagery that distract from the tension. While the institutional obstruction creates superb pressure, the climax in Chapter 22 feels slightly compressed, resolving a m",
